From a429bcfa2948cdcb6eb87739826d01dba813152c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/43] usb_webcam: add the UVC control helpers and their tests

UVCControls.h lists the controls of the processing unit and the
camera terminal of UVC 1.0 that the parameter web will offer
(brightness, contrast, hue, saturation, sharpness, gamma, white
balance, backlight compensation, gain, power line frequency and
exposure), and holds the conversions it needs: little endian values
of 1, 2 or 4 bytes, signed or not, the pairs of the white balance
component control, rounding and clamping a slider value to the range
the camera reports, choosing an exposure mode the camera supports,
and checking a control transfer's length.

Nothing uses it yet; the next change builds the parameters from it.
It is separate to keep each change reviewable. UVCControlsTest
covers the conversions.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit ee1479d9d96561027339f7f242bb7669ee895334)
---
